{
    "_notes": "TDK InvenSense ICM-20948 9-axis IMU at 0x69 (AD0 high, the Adafruit and SparkFun default); 0x68 with AD0 low isn't claimed, as MCP342x ADCs there take any byte written as their configuration (as the AMG8833 record). The record covers the accelerometer, gyroscope and temperature; the AK09916 magnetometer inside is reached through the chip's own I2C master, which isn't set up. 8-bit registers in four banks, chosen by REG_BANK_SEL (0x7F)\nDetection: WHO_AM_I (bank 0, 0x00) = 0xEA\nInit: bank 0; PWR_MGMT_1 (0x06) = 0x80 - reset, 100 ms; PWR_MGMT_1 = 0x01 - awake, best clock, 50 ms; bank 2: GYRO_CONFIG_1 (0x01) = 0x03 - +/-500 dps, low-pass filter on; ACCEL_CONFIG (0x14) = 0x03 - +/-4 g, low-pass filter on; back to bank 0\nPoll (100 ms): ACCEL_XOUT_H to TEMP_OUT_L (0x2D-0x3A), big-endian 16-bit: accelerometer 8192 per g, gyro 65.5 per dps, temperature = count / 333.87 + 21 degC\nSource: registers from the TDK ICM-20948 datasheet",
    "addresses": "0x69",
